	<key>recovery.helper</key>
	<string>Closed-lid mode normally asks for administrator permission each time it is enabled. To avoid repeated prompts, click Install in the Helper row below Keep awake with lid closed. macOS will request administrator permission. The helper never knows or stores your password.

To manage an installed helper, click Configure… in the same row. You can switch back to password prompts or remove the helper there. Stop Wakecup before updating or removing it. Installation, updates and removal require administrator permission; ordinary use with a working helper does not. If the Helper row shows Update after an app update, click it before enabling closed-lid mode again.

The helper is available to the Mac user who installed it. It starts a protective process for closed-lid mode and restores normal sleep when the mode stops. Removing it preserves information needed to recover an interrupted mode.</string>
